 docs/EDGE_SUNDAY_RUNBOOK.md | 14 ++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 14 insertions(+)

diff --git a/docs/EDGE_SUNDAY_RUNBOOK.md b/docs/EDGE_SUNDAY_RUNBOOK.md
index 9b6cee5..48a78b4 100644
--- a/docs/EDGE_SUNDAY_RUNBOOK.md
+++ b/docs/EDGE_SUNDAY_RUNBOOK.md
@@ -10,6 +10,14 @@ stored forecasts, quotes, reports or grades; never rerun a game after kickoff. O
 `arbsims edge stage --stage publish` (approved budget about 84 per Sunday: EDGE_RUN_CREDITS 100, EDGE_WEEKLY_CREDITS 120).
 Every other command runs with `env -u ODDS_API_KEY`. No automatic retries of a failed publish stage.
 
+**Website export (owner-approved 2026-10-30, Phase 2; read-only, 0 credits).** The last step of each section below
+exports what that section already stored, for the ArbitrEdge V5 website: `arbsims web-export` opens the database
+read-only and writes one new `sims_nfl_*.json.gz` file to `$SCRATCH/web_export`, which is uploaded with
+`gh release upload web-export <file>` (create the release once with `gh release create web-export --prerelease
+--title "SIMS web exports (do not delete)" --notes "Read-only NFL exports for the V5 website"`). It never changes a
+forecast, report, grade or the ledger, and runs only after the section's own steps are complete. If it fails,
+report it in one line and do nothing else (never rerun the section's earlier steps because of it).
+
 ## Saturday ~18:47 CT: prepare (0 credits)
 1. `env -u ODDS_API_KEY .venv/bin/python scripts/free_refresh.py` (free nflverse data).
 2. `env -u ODDS_API_KEY .venv/bin/python -m arbsims.cli edge plan` -> tomorrow's Sunday game ids (America/Chicago).
@@ -22,6 +30,8 @@ Every other command runs with `env -u ODDS_API_KEY`. No automatic retries of a f
    (`forecast.designate(..., by="owner")`, reason citing the owner's 2026-10-30 approval of the Sunday report system).
 4. `env -u ODDS_API_KEY .venv/bin/python -m arbsims.cli edge stage --stage prepare` (records readiness).
 5. `arbsims ledger sync`; commit locally; report in a few lines.
+6. Website export: `env -u ODDS_API_KEY .venv/bin/python -m arbsims.cli web-export projections --week <week> --out $SCRATCH/web_export`,
+   then upload the new file (see the top).
 
 ## Sunday 9:15 CT: collect, validate, publish (<= ~84 credits)
 1. `.venv/bin/python -m arbsims.cli edge stage --stage publish` (WITH the odds key; this is the only paid call).
@@ -32,9 +42,13 @@ Every other command runs with `env -u ODDS_API_KEY`. No automatic retries of a f
 4. Report: picks (player, side, line, book, calibrated ROI, raw simulated %), credits used and remaining (from the
    report meta), warnings and excluded games. Must be done before 10:00 CT; say so if it was not.
 5. `arbsims ledger sync`; commit locally.
+6. Website export: `env -u ODDS_API_KEY .venv/bin/python -m arbsims.cli web-export edges --out $SCRATCH/web_export` and
+   `... web-export projections --week <week> --out $SCRATCH/web_export`, then upload the new files (see the top).
 
 ## Tuesday ~7:48 CT: grade (0 credits)
 1. `env -u ODDS_API_KEY .venv/bin/python scripts/free_refresh.py`.
 2. `env -u ODDS_API_KEY .venv/bin/python -m arbsims.cli edge stage --stage grade --slate <last Sunday>`.
 3. Re-render and republish the page (history updates); report the week's graded Top 5 and running totals with the
    sample-size warning. Commit locally.
+4. Website export: `env -u ODDS_API_KEY .venv/bin/python -m arbsims.cli web-export history --out $SCRATCH/web_export`, then upload
+   the new file (see the top).
